<speak>I have actually been spending time in the garden. It is pleasant to have something to do that cannot be hurried by sending another email. I used to walk past a neglected corner and think that I should ask somebody to sort it out. Recently I cleared it myself and discovered that I enjoyed the work. My wife was amused because I came indoors looking very satisfied with something that, to everyone else, simply looked like a tidier patch of ground. I had spent so much of my working life discussing things other people would do that the physical result felt quite different.</speak>